module

public import Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Perm
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Subgroup.Defs

/-!
# A candidate orbital graph for the fixed Held action

Starting from the words recorded in `Normalizer/Source/lower_words.json`,
take the orbit of letter 1 under the subgroup fixing letter 0, and transport
that set along a spanning tree for the two original Held generators.
The result is stored as binary row masks, with zero-based letter indices.
`Normalizer/Source/generate_graph.py` reproduces this table from the retained
ATLAS `HeG1-p2058B0` files.

This module defines the finite relation and its full group of preserving
permutations. Identification with the 425-suborbit relation, preservation
by the full Held normalizer, and a bound on the preserving group are separate
proof obligations. None is asserted by the data definition.
-/

namespace Held.NormalizerGraph

